# Expo React Native Development Standards

## Component Structure
- Always write React functional components using arrow function syntax: `() => {}`
- Never use function declarations for components
- Use TypeScript for all components with proper typing

## Project Organization
- Create reusable components in a `components/` folder at the root level
- Organize components by feature or functionality within subdirectories
- Use PascalCase for component file names (e.g., `UserProfile.tsx`)
- Export components as default exports

## Code Style
- Use arrow functions for all React components
- Prefer const over let/var for component declarations
- Use destructuring for props and state
- Always include proper TypeScript types for props

## Example Component Structure
```tsx
interface ComponentProps {
  title: string;
  onPress?: () => void;
}

const MyComponent = ({ title, onPress }: ComponentProps) => {
  return (
    // JSX here
  );
};

export default MyComponent;
```

## File Organization
- App screens go in `app/` directory (Expo Router structure)
- Reusable components go in `components/` directory
- Types and interfaces in separate files or at the top of component files
- Use index files for cleaner imports when appropriate

## React Native Best Practices
- Use Expo's built-in components and APIs when available
- Follow React Native performance best practices
- Use proper key props for lists
- Handle platform differences appropriately